# C++ naming

Layout → [structure.mdc](structure.mdc). Python: [../python/naming.mdc](../python/naming.mdc). Bash: [../bash/naming.mdc](../bash/naming.mdc).

A prefix describes **behavior type**, not decoration. Applies to **new code** — do not refactor legacy unless asked.

## Prefixes (methods)

| Prefix | Returns | Meaning | Good example | Bad example |
|--------|---------|---------|--------------|-------------|
| `Is` | `bool` | “is X true now?” | `IsReady()` | `IsVelocity()` returning `int` |
| `Has` | `bool` | “does it exist / is it available?” | `HasActiveSession()` | `HasVelocity` when the value is not a bool |
| `Get` | a value | read with no state change | `GetOutputValue()` | `GetAndSend()` — side effect |
| `Set` | `void` or `bool` | write / configure | `SetOutputValues()` | `SetVelocity` when it only reads |
| `Try` | `bool` / `optional` | failure is a normal path | `TryClearErrors()` | `TryStop` when it always succeeds |

`Set` — **methods only**, never a class field. `has_errors` = “errors exist”; `IsInErrorState` = “we are in an error state”. Optional `Can` for permission (“is this allowed?”).

Also: `Wait`, `Check`, `On`, `Parse`, `Create`/`Make`, `Require`/`Ensure`.

No prefix when the name is an **action** or a **transform**: `Stop()`, `Activate()`, `RpmToLinearVelocity`.

## Fields vs methods

Prefixes `Is` / `Has` / `Get` / `Set` / `Try` go on **methods**. Fields are **data**:

```cpp
// Bool fields — adjective / participle, no is_/has_; trailing _
std::atomic<bool> connection_active_{false};
bool active_{false};  // CanDevice: Activate() completed; compound name when context is narrow
std::atomic<bool> enable_requested_{false};
std::atomic<bool> command_loop_running_{false};

// Methods — Is/Has prefix on methods, not on fields
bool IsConnectionActive() const { return connection_active_.load(); }
bool IsActive() const { return active_; }
bool SetOutputValues(int32_t ch1, int32_t ch2);

// Local bools — is_/has_ OK
const bool is_pending_activation = ...;
```

Bad on a field: `is_active_`, `is_activated_`, `set_active_`. Good: `enable_requested_` (request) vs `active_` / `connection_active_` (state). Legacy names in review comments or old code — use the field pattern above in **new** code.

Legacy `is_*_` fields — do not refactor unless asked; **new** fields without `is_`.

## Name = actual role

- The name describes **what it is**, not what you “meant to achieve”.
  - Good: `GetInterfaceName()`
  - Bad: `ClaimName()` — this is not a “claim”
- **Bool names must state a concrete fact**, not a vague grade.
  - Good: `all_motors_activated`, `steering_activated`, `all_bms_activated`, `all_brakes_activated`, `hv_transition_succeeded`
  - Bad: `ok`, `all_ok`, `motors_ok`, `success`, `status_ok`, `result`, `any_activated` when the contract is “every device” — reader cannot tell *what* is true
  - Prefer participle / predicate over empty intensifiers (`all` alone, `ok`, `fine`, `good`). Use `any_*` only when the bool truly means “at least one”.
- **Same terminology** throughout the file (`account`, not `user` if the rest uses `accounts_`).
- **Existing pattern in the file** wins: `ConnectionStateToString` → new enums also `FooToString`, not `HardwareStateName`.
- Enum: short values (`STOPPED`, `ACTIVE`, `INACTIVE`) instead of compound ones (`SAFE_STOPPED`) when they add no information.
- New state enum: `enum class Foo` + `FooToString()` in the same `.hpp` — details in [structure.mdc](structure.mdc).
- Domain-bool: `resource_locked_`, not a vague `drive_permitted` when it is a lock.
- Keep names short, but do not compress words into a private shorthand: `GetTerminalWidth`, not `GetTermWidth`. Established acronyms (`ROS`, `URI`, `XML`) are fine.

## Exclusions

Do not change external framework APIs or overrides required by a base class.
